From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:17:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): each camera's threshold, and Test shows each
 camera's score, anti-spoofing's and the one-face check

The settings know recognition.ir_threshold (the IR camera's; null: the
threshold) and anti_spoofing.pair_max_offset / pair_max_size_ratio
(both cameras must see one face), with the helper's defaults in
defaults.yaml. A Thresholds block puts the colour camera's and the IR
camera's recognition thresholds and the anti-spoofing model's side by
side (finer steps, 0.01), each marked as used or not in the mode, the
IR one "same as colour" until it is moved; it warns below 0.6. Choosing
a mode raises an IR threshold of its own below 0.6, as it does the
colour one. The model sections keep only the model choices.

Test reads more of the helper's log: each camera's last result (best
score, its threshold, matched), the anti-spoofing score against its
threshold, whether both cameras saw one face, and each face's score
with the threshold it was compared against, so a face's badge is red
against its own camera's threshold.
Tests: scan (per face, per camera, spoof and pair lines), faceMode.test.ts.
